  "details": "The expression \"join requests\" should be replaced with \"invite requests\" if they are in the context of joining a world instance. (Note. \"join requests\" is also used in the context of joining a Group.)\n\nSee the attached image. I believe These \"join requests\" means \"invite requests\". And there seems to be no explanation of this term in docs. So, it should be revised.\n\n- 23677 `Auto-accept join requests`\n\n- 23681 `See join requests`\n\n- 23685 `Hide location, see join requests`\n\n- 23689 `Hide location, hide join requests`\n\n# note\n\n1: The following strings are for the context of joining a Group. They are out of the scope of this post. They have the \"groups\" tag properly.\n\n- 35066 `Join request cancelled`\n\n- 35082 `Cancel Join Request`\n\n2: I issued an inverted thing on Crowdin 4 months ago for\n\n13413 `Cancel a pending invite request`\n\nThis `invite request` should be `group join request`.",
